## v44 — sword and dash moves rebuilt on the animation principles
Source: the AnimationTutorial1–3 docs and the firytwig reference sheets.

Rebuilt in place, **Sword**: slash 1, slash 2, combo 3-hit, combo 5-hit, thrust, thrust rush, rising slash, overhead smash, guard crush, spin slash, air slash, plunge, iai draw, dash slash, launcher, feint, crouch cut, air combo. **Dash / mobility**: Run · start, Run · skid stop, Dash · forward burst, Dash · step in, Backstep, Slide. Other categories unchanged and still on the older poses.

### Recipe format
`[name, category, duration_ms, default_steps, frames]`. A frame is either `"pose"` (tween on, recipe steps) or `[pose, steps, ease, hold]` — `steps` = in-betweens into the next key (0 = cut straight to it), `ease` = linear / in / out / inout / in3 / out3 / snap, `hold` = extra frames the key stays on screen. `duration_ms = 0` means frame count × `FRAME_MS`.

### Timing pattern
ready → chamber (hold 1–3, in-betweens bunched with `in3`) → breakdown → overshoot (no ease into the hit) → ease out to the hit pose → hold → eased recovery.

### Pose rules (sw2_*, dash2_*)
Knees and elbows bend only the anatomical way; feet grounded and the rear foot planted through lunges; `wp` within ±180 and every tweened segment under 180° per joint, with `bd_*` breakdowns inserted where a swing would take the long way round.

### Engine/tool changes carried since v44
`_tween.hold` (0–24) with holds baked on export; `in3` / `out3` eases; the film strip shows `~steps =hold`; `tplFrames()` shared by `applyTPL` and `mkAction`.

### Finding (render probe)
Many original atlas poses (`stand_ready`, `crouch_idle`, `run_*`, `jump_crouch`) have the rear knee bending backwards. Untouched — outside the scope of the reworks so far.

## Notes
- Pose angle convention: limbs 0 = straight down, positive = toward the facing direction (+x). Spine 0 = up. Weapon world angle `wang = rua + rfa + wp` (0 up, 90 forward, 180 down).
